            <ArticleTitle>IGF2 revs the steroidogenesis engine.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>C19-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1530/ERC-13-0243</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Molecular understanding of how prostate cancers evade hormone therapy greatly increased over the last several years, and the realization that de novo steroidogenesis plays a significant role in tumor progression and therapeutic bypass has led to development of promising new therapeutics. In the April 2013 issue of Endocrine-Related Cancer, Lubik et al. revealed a new molecular pathway by which the IGF2 can ignite the de novo steroidogenesis engine and promote molecular events associated with tumor progression.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
